<BaseLayout title="Knowledge Center – Learn Acupressure" description="Everything you need to know about acupressure: fundamentals, condition-specific protocols, techniques, research evidence, and safety guidelines." breadcrumbs={[{ label: "Home", href: "/" }, { label: "Learning Center", href: "/learn" }]}>
<div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 py-12 lg:px-6"><h1 class="mb-3">Knowledge Center</h1><p class="text-stone-500 dark:text-stone-400 text-lg mb-10">Everything you should know before practicing acupressure — from fundamental concepts to advanced techniques and clinical evidence.</p><section class="mb-10">
<h2 class="text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-stone-900 dark:text-stone-100 mb-3">What You'll Find Here</h2>
<p class="text-stone-600 dark:text-stone-300 leading-relaxed mb-3">Acupressure is a therapeutic technique rooted in Traditional Chinese Medicine (TCM) that applies firm pressure to specific points on the body, called acupoints, which lie along energy pathways known as meridians. Unlike acupuncture, acupressure works entirely on the surface — no skin is broken — so it can be practiced with your fingers, thumbs, elbows, or simple tools anywhere you have a few quiet minutes.</p>
<p class="text-stone-600 dark:text-stone-300 leading-relaxed mb-3">This center gathers everything on the site into one starting point. The Basics section explains what acupressure is, how it works, and what the research says about its benefits. The Conditions pages give step-by-step point protocols for common problems such as headaches, back pain, nausea, anxiety, and poor sleep. Techniques covers proper form, Research summarizes the clinical evidence, and Safety explains when to be cautious and who should avoid certain points.</p>
<p class="text-stone-600 dark:text-stone-300 leading-relaxed">You do not have to read everything before you begin. If you want to start pressing points today, open How to Do Acupressure at Home, then look up a single point in the Body Atlas. Use the rest of the sections when you want to go deeper or target a specific condition.</p>
</section>
